                <note rend="inline" type="source">668.113C.P./2: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Skinner</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-03-04T17:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 4, 1927—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>8. Emergency Fleet Corporation has been informed by operators of Shipping Board
                    vessels that Greek Government has or is about to promulgate further restriction
                    import regulations on flour. Please investigate and report by telegraph.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
